  "description": "DOVCAU crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P c a 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C68 H112 Cu2 N4 O40 Tb7 5+,6(H2 O1),5(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb7 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.401-3.973 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.10-132.08°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Cu2Tb7(OH)10(teaH)2(teaH3)2(O2CPh)6(MeOH)2(H2O)4]Cl5·6H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 10 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 10 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Cu(II), Tb(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
